          "a": "Count islands (connected '1's horizontally or vertically) in a 2D binary grid using DFS/BFS sink technique.",
          "e": "Iterate over grid. On finding '1', increment island count and run DFS mutating all adjacent '1's to '0'.",
          "code": "public class Main {\n    public static int numIslands(char[][] grid) {\n        int count = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < grid.length; i++) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < grid[0].length; j++) {\n                if (grid[i][j] == '1') {\n                    count++;\n                    dfs(grid, i, j);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return count;\n    }\n    static void dfs(char[][] grid, int r, int c) {\n        if (r < 0 || r >= grid.length || c < 0 || c >= grid[0].length || grid[r][c] != '1') return;\n        grid[r][c] = '0';\n        dfs(grid, r+1, c); dfs(grid, r-1, c); dfs(grid, r, c+1); dfs(grid, r, c-1);\n    }\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        char[][] grid = {{'1','1','0'},{'1','1','0'},{'0','0','1'}};\n        System.out.println(\"Islands: \" + numIslands(grid));\n    }\n}",
