          "level": "I",
          "q": "Explain Java Garbage Collection generations: Eden, Survivor, Tenured, Metaspace.",
          "a": "The heap is divided into Young and Old generations based on the Weak Generational Hypothesis (most objects die young). Young contains Eden, S0, and S1. Surviving objects move between S0/S1 via Minor GC and age up. Once threshold (default 15) is reached, they promote to Old Generation (Tenured). Metaspace holds class metadata in native off-heap memory.",
          "e": "Minor GC cleans Young Generation (fast, Stop-The-World is very brief). Major/Full GC cleans Old Generation. Modern GCs like G1, ZGC, and Shenandoah use regional partitioning for sub-millisecond pauses.",
