          "q": "Comparable vs Comparator: difference and modern lambda usage?",
          "a": "Comparable<T> defines the natural ordering of a class by implementing int compareTo(T o). Comparator<T> defines external custom ordering logic using int compare(T o1, T o2). A class can have only one natural ordering, but multiple custom Comparators.",
