          "q": "Java 8 Streams: Intermediate vs Terminal operations and lazy evaluation?",
          "a": "Intermediate operations (filter, map, flatMap, sorted, distinct) return a new Stream and are lazily evaluated—no computation occurs until a terminal operation is called. Terminal operations (collect, forEach, reduce, count, anyMatch) trigger traversal and consume the stream.",
          "e": "Streams fuse operations into a single pass over the data, avoiding intermediate collection allocations. Streams cannot be reused once terminated.",
