          "a": "Platform threads map 1:1 to OS kernel threads, consuming ~1MB stack memory and requiring expensive kernel context switches (limiting concurrency to thousands). Virtual threads are lightweight user-mode threads managed by JVM (Project Loom), consuming ~few KBs. When a virtual thread executes blocking I/O, the JVM unmounts it from its OS carrier thread.",
