          "q": "Database Indexing: B-Tree vs Hash index, clustered vs non-clustered, leftmost prefix rule?",
          "a": "B-Tree indices store sorted data in balanced tree nodes, supporting range queries (<, >) and sorting (O(log N)). Hash index supports exact lookups (O(1)) but cannot do range queries. Clustered index determines physical storage order of table rows (one per table, usually Primary Key). Non-clustered index stores index key with pointer to row ID.",
