          "a": "CAP: In a distributed system with Network Partitions (P), you must choose between Consistency (C - all nodes see same data simultaneously) or Availability (A - every request gets non-error response). CP systems (HBase, MongoDB, ZooKeeper) favor consistency; AP systems (Cassandra, DynamoDB) favor availability.",
