          "q": "Distributed Locking: Redis Redlock algorithm vs ZooKeeper?",
          "a": "Single-node Redis SET key uuid NX PX 30000 provides basic locking, but if master crashes before replication, another client can acquire the same lock. Redlock algorithm acquires locks across N independent Redis masters sequentially with strict timeouts. ZooKeeper uses sequential ephemeral znodes: the lowest sequence number holds lock, others set watches on the node immediately preceding them.",
