          "q": "How does Spring @Transactional work under the hood and why does self-invocation fail?",
          "a": "Spring uses dynamic proxies (JDK dynamic proxy or CGLIB). When a method annotated with @Transactional is called from another bean, the proxy intercepts the call, starts a DB transaction, invokes target method, commits if successful, and rolls back on RuntimeException. If methodA() calls methodB() within the same class (self-invocation), the call bypasses the proxy, and @Transactional is completely ignored.",
