      "code": "public class Test {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        int i = 0;\n        i = i++;\n        System.out.println(i);\n    }\n}",
      "options": [
        "0",
        "1",
        "2",
        "Compilation Error"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "explanation": "i++ evaluates to the old value (0) and queues the increment. Then the assignment '=' writes the old value 0 back into i, overwriting the increment! Hence i remains 0."
